# Imperial Dominion Online
#
# Defence in depth for the plugin directory, and nothing more than that.
#
# This file works on Apache and LiteSpeed. **nginx ignores it completely**, so
# nothing here may ever be the only thing between a request and something that
# matters. What actually keeps the plugin safe works on every server: every PHP
# file refuses to run unless WordPress loaded it, every file under tests/ and
# tools/ refuses to run unless a command line started it, and uninstall.php runs
# only during an uninstall.
#
# What this is for is the installation nobody planned: a zip of the repository
# rather than a built release. That carries the test suite and the design docs,
# and if somebody archived their own working copy rather than using GitHub's
# download button, the entire .git directory with every version of every file
# that was ever committed.
#
# Two deliberate omissions:
#
# "Options -Indexes" is not here. On a host that allows .htaccess but not
# Options, it returns 500 for the whole plugin, which is a worse failure than
# the directory listing it would have prevented. The index.php files in every
# directory do that job instead and behave the same on every server.
#
# <FilesMatch> with Require or Deny is not here either, for the same class of
# reason: those need AllowOverride to grant Limit or AuthConfig, and where it
# does not, the result is 500 on every request rather than a rule that quietly
# does nothing. Everything below is mod_alias, which needs only FileInfo, the
# one override class a host that allows .htaccess at all almost always grants.

<IfModule mod_alias.c>

    # Anything inside a dot-directory, .git above all.
    #
    # A path rule rather than a filename rule, because the files inside .git are
    # named "config", "HEAD" and "index": no rule matching dotted *filenames*
    # would catch a single one of them. Matching a dot straight after a slash
    # catches the directory and everything beneath it, and cannot match an
    # ordinary path, because a normal URL never has one.
    RedirectMatch 404 /\.

    # Readable text that is not meant to be served: the schema, the
    # documentation, and any tooling manifest or editor leftover.
    #
    # The schema is the one with any weight. It is public on GitHub, so it is no
    # secret, but it names every table and column, which is the first thing
    # worth having if an injection point ever turned up, and there is no reason
    # to hand it to anyone who asks.
    RedirectMatch 404 \.(sql|md|json|ya?ml|lock|dist|ini|log|sh|bak|orig|rej|swp)$

</IfModule>
